From 3122c2bfe1970223e022d235873680b479b3a562 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: keyspark <kevin.on.the.rocks@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 08:13:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] DSpark port: ngram context drafting, redraft on miss,
 per-position margin stop

--dspark-ngram N extends the MTP chain with suffix-ngram (prompt-lookup)
proposals from the committed context, replacing the role of DSpark's learned
Markov head, which the MTP GGUF does not ship. A low-margin second MTP token
is truncated instead of aborting when the context can extend past the
verified-for-free drafts[0], and a position-0 MTP miss redrafts from the
target's own greedy token. --dspark-early-margin F stops the recursive chain
at the first unsure position so deep chains avoid the partial-accept replay
verify. --dspark-rounds is parsed but not implemented yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
